course: dictionary
lesson: 2915
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as 1), 2) and 3). To choose the right one, read the sentence around the word. Those words are its context, and they leave clues. «A boy in Arizona wants a bearded dragon for his birthday.» There is no fire and no castle here, so dragon means a real lizard that can be a pet.
explain: «The dragon guarded the treasure and breathed fire at the knight.» Guarding treasure and breathing fire belong to stories, so this dragon is a made-up creature. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words are used as jokes. If someone says, «My coach is a dragon when we are late», the clues are late and shouting, so dragon means a fierce, strict person. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A dragon is a made-up creature in stories, usually a huge lizard-like monster with wings and claws that can breathe fire.
fact: Dragon is also the name of some real lizards, like the Komodo dragon and the bearded dragon.
fact: The Komodo dragon is the biggest living lizard, up to about 3 metres long, and it lives on a few islands in Indonesia.
fact: In Chinese tradition the dragon is lucky and kind, and dragon dances happen at Chinese New Year.
fact: «Dragon» can also mean a fierce, strict person, said as a joke.
exercise: «A boy in Arizona wants a bearded dragon for his birthday.» Which dragon is meant? | A fierce, strict person | A knight in armour | A made-up creature with wings | *A real lizard that can be a pet
exercise: «The dragon guarded the treasure and breathed fire at the knight.» What kind of dragon is this? | A fierce, strict teacher | A lucky dragon dance at New Year | *A made-up creature in a story | A real lizard from Indonesia
exercise: «Our coach is a real dragon when we are late, shouting at everyone.» What does dragon mean here? | *A fierce, strict person, said as a joke | A creature that brings rain | A kind Chinese dragon | A real lizard
test: «The Komodo dragon is the biggest living lizard in the world.» Which meaning of dragon is this? | A lucky dragon dance | A made-up creature with wings | *A real lizard | A fierce, strict person
test: In Chinese tradition, what is the dragon like? | *Lucky and kind, and it brings rain | A lizard that lives in Wales | A cruel monster that steals gold | A knight's horse
exam: A child says, «My dad is such a dragon when the bins are not out.» What does dragon mean here? | *A fierce, strict person, said as a joke | A real lizard | A dragon dance at New Year | A made-up monster with wings
